## 1 · Diagnose (`diagnosis.md`)

Inspected both planes against the installed alpha.2 host and reproduced the baseline on isolated profiles. The baseline *composes* (the row is scanned into `globalThis["__DSH_BOOT__"]`), so all breakages are contract-level and silent at host boot. Card ids and pinned evidence:

| Card id | Breakage |
|---|---|
| `client-inject-list` | `dsh.client.inject` named the retired `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime` + pre-`ui-renderer` providers, and omitted the packages that own `slots`/`locale`/`settings.section` |
| `locale-namespace-declaration` | the typed 2-arg `ctx.locale.register(ns, {zh,en})` form used without merging the namespace into `LocaleNamespaceMap` |
| `peer-cohort` | bare `cordis` + `^0.1.0-rc.5` peers, including two packages retired in this cohort |
| `dead-type-sources` | JSDoc imported `cordis` and `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-runtime/client`; the real type surface then also rejected the host `ctx.effect` body returning `void` |

Also documented: an image-wide live-reload defect (alpha.2 launcher calls `hmr.registerConfig()`, image ships `cordis-plugin-hmr@1.0.19` without it) proven with a **no-plugin control**, and the unsafe `pnpm publish --force` release step.

## 2 · Fix (`/app/fixture`, uncommitted)

- `package.json` — cohort-correct inject list (`ui-renderer`/`ui-settings`/`client-locale`), restated peers (`@deepseek-ai/cordis ^4.0.2`, `^0.1.2-alpha.2`), `./client` types wiring, `ui-slots` devDependency, **version `0.1.2` → `0.1.2-alpha.2`**
- `client.d.ts` (new) — merges `'dsh-plugin-mcp-manager': 'heading' | 'add'` into `LocaleNamespaceMap` and carries the client type surface
- `client.js` / `index.js` — scoped `@deepseek-ai/cordis` context types, retired memo removed, effect now returns its disposer
- `README.md` — verify-then-publish procedure; no publish performed (`private: true`)

## 3 · Deploy

Fresh isolated `DSH_HOME`, `dsh plugin --profile web add file:/app/fixture`, cold boot:

- host half applied both effects; tree settled with no activation failure (`--dump-config` composes the row)
- the announced boot graph lists `@bench/dsh-bench-mcpanel` with the migrated inject list, and the row's bundle URL serves `200` (1956 bytes)
- extra verification: `tsc --allowJs --checkJs` against the real cohort packages exits **0**
- deploy run used `patchReload: "startup"` because the image's live HMR path fails host-wide (control logs included)

Caveats recorded in §7–9: no browser (roster is the anchor), the client *build* wrapper is elided in the fixture, and the vendored upgrade corpus (`/opt/dsh-migrate-skills`) is absent, so upstream full card ids could not be quoted — the corridor slugs above are pinned to file/line evidence instead.

